url: "https://mzyphur.github.io/gas-tax/"
abstract: >-
  Forensic accounting of Australia's offshore-gas fiscal regime —
  Petroleum Resource Rent Tax, company income tax, state royalties,
  and the grandfathered North West Shelf Commonwealth royalty —
  against Budget 2026-27 and against the
  fiscal-architecture documents of Norway, Qatar, the United States,
  the United Kingdom, Malaysia, and Japan (the latter as the
  destination-market angle). Quantifies the gap between Australia's
  per-tonne state take (~A$49/t) and Norway's (~A$491/t), Qatar's
  (~A$725/t), and the United States' (~A$61/t); enumerates what a
  25 per cent levy on the gross value of LNG exports would raise
  (~A$17 bn/yr) and what current Australian budget costings show
  that figure would fund.
